# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true, which checks every text file out
# with CRLF. Parts of the unit suite read source files as text (to compare the
# web front-end with the server, to check a shipped script), so a CRLF checkout
# changed what those tests saw. Source is LF in the repository and stays LF in
# every working tree, whatever core.autocrlf says. `text=auto` keeps git's
# binary detection, so a binary file added under these folders is left alone.
src/** text=auto eol=lf
web/** text=auto eol=lf
# Shell scripts run inside Linux/WSL straight from this checkout (e.g. /mnt/d/...): a CRLF
# checkout breaks bash with "$'': command not found".
*.sh text eol=lf
